# Pluto notebooks (Styx)

**Bootstrap only when the user requests notebook work.**

## Skills

- **styx-setup** — install, Julia prerequisite, MCP troubleshooting (before notebook work)
- **pluto-session** — start Pluto, open notebook, Glass navigation
- **pluto-workflow** — cell edits once a notebook is open
- **pluto-semantics** — cell structure (`imports_cell`, `begin`/`end` blocks, `@bind`) and parse-error fixes

Never ask the user to run `pluto-serve.sh`. Prefer `start_pluto_session` / `open_notebook` **by name** even if not in the MCP tool picker. On **Remote SSH**, if that would start a laptop Pluto, the agent starts `PlutoMCP.serve()` in the **workspace Shell** instead (see **pluto-session** `remote-ssh.md`).

## Bootstrap

Notebook intent → **pluto-session** first. Glass: **`cursor-ide-browser`** (`position: "active"`; view ID `glass-browser-*`). Path B: after `open_notebook`, `browser_click` notebook on landing — not pasted `/edit?id=`. **Not** `plugin-browse-browser`. **Remote SSH:** start Pluto on the SSH host (see **pluto-session** `remote-ssh.md`); Cursor auto-forwards ports — do not boot a laptop Pluto.

## Safe preview

Path B default = **Safe preview**. Remind user to click **Run notebook code** in Glass — still edit when asked. Detection signals → **pluto-workflow**.

## Cell edits (notebook open)

Design Mode (**⌘⇧D**) → **`resolve_pluto_context`** → **`read_cell`** → stage → **`submit_changes`** → re-read.

Re-read before overwriting browser drafts. **`submit_changes`** before ending turn if staged.
